The change belongs in one file. `SftAlgorithm.shape_sample_row` in `reef/train/slime_backend/sft.py` (line 38) decides the reward. It checks `"reward" in sample.metadata`, so a key that holds `null` still reaches `trajectory_reward`, which raises. The fix is to test for a non-null value instead, so a null reward falls back to 0.0 and a present reward is still checked for finiteness. I did not read the test files or make the edit.

`reef/core/trajectories.py` (`trajectory_reward`) should stay as it is, because a present reward must still be finite. The other candidates from the index are recipe or sample-building files, but the failure happens when the row is shaped, so they are not needed.

