The change belongs in the dispatcher. `list_artifacts` and `locked_scenario` return the loaded instance without checking whether control has committed past it. `_file_scenario` in `request_service.py` already does this check for file reads. It calls `follow_commits` when `runs_control` is false, so the same guard is missing from these two methods.

I did not write any change. The main file is `reef/dispatcher/dispatcher.py`. `list_artifacts` (line 496) and `locked_scenario` (line 772) need the `runs_control` check and `follow_commits`, as `_file_scenario` does. `reef/service/request_service.py` holds the reference pattern, and `reef/service/routes/scenarios.py` is the caller of `list_artifacts`. I did not confirm the route's exact dependency on the dispatcher, so it is listed only as a possible touch point.

