The error comes from `EvaluationResults.settle` in `reef/service/artifact_evaluations.py`. When a rollout of a deleted scenario is read from the queue, `settle` calls `self.dispatcher.locked_scenario(scenario)`, which raises `UnknownScenario` (a `ReefError`, `reef/core/errors.py:16`). Nothing in `settle` catches it. It propagates to the `logger.exception("could not end evaluation ...")` handler in `read_results` (lines 200-204), which logs a traceback. The fix is to return quietly from `settle` when the scenario is unknown. I did not write the change.

The test-side change (stopping the samples service in the record copy test) touches only tests, so it is outside this list.

